Build the tantivy binding with the cargo on PATH instead of a rustup toolchain.

Upstream's CMake runs `cargo +1.89 build`; the +toolchain argument is a
rustup selector that only the rustup proxy binaries understand. The Debian 13
package build installs rustc and cargo from the versioned dhi.io packages, so
there is no rustup and `cargo +1.89` fails with "no such command". Dropping
the selector runs the cargo find_program resolved, whose version the package
definition pins and tracks.

Upstream CMake: https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/blob/v2.6.23/internal/core/thirdparty/tantivy/CMakeLists.txt
rustup toolchain override syntax: https://rust-lang.github.io/rustup/overrides.html

diff --git a/internal/core/thirdparty/tantivy/CMakeLists.txt b/internal/core/thirdparty/tantivy/CMakeLists.txt
index 36663e6..02e2c00 100644
--- a/internal/core/thirdparty/tantivy/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/internal/core/thirdparty/tantivy/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -11,10 +11,10 @@ find_program(CARGO_EXECUTABLE
         REQUIRED)
 
 if (CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE STREQUAL "Debug")
-    set(CARGO_CMD ${CARGO_EXECUTABLE} +1.89 build --verbose)
+    set(CARGO_CMD ${CARGO_EXECUTABLE} build --verbose)
     set(TARGET_DIR "debug")
 else ()
-    set(CARGO_CMD ${CARGO_EXECUTABLE} +1.89 build --release --verbose)
+    set(CARGO_CMD ${CARGO_EXECUTABLE} build --release --verbose)
     set(TARGET_DIR "release")
 endif ()
 
